Result: Partial. Infra, CI/CD, container, Render and Cloudflare files were read fully. `tests/databricks/*`, `pyproject.toml` and `Makefile` were not read, because the 12-call budget ran out after the first batch. Line numbers below were counted by hand from the tool output and may be off by one in the longer files. Secret values are not printed.

Findings:
- `.github/workflows/orchestrate.yml:89` — `create_repo(... repo_type='dataset', exist_ok=True)` has no `private=True`, and line 90 uploads `data/lake`. The de-identified Silver/Gold lake goes to HF dataset `swadhinbiswas/eustream`, which is public by default. That is outside AWS eu-central-1 and outside the IaC residency claim. HIGH, residency/exposure.
- `.github/workflows/orchestrate.yml:22` — The DuckDB warehouse (`data/eurocart.duckdb`), `data/events.db` and `governance/pii_manifest.json` (lines 22-24) are stored in the GitHub Actions cache. Runner and cache region is not controlled by the IaC, and the warehouse may hold PII (the pipeline hashes PII, so scope is uncertain). MEDIUM, residency.
- `.github/workflows/orchestrate.yml:4` — `cron: "0 */4 * * *"` runs every 4 hours. Line 6 also runs the full pipeline on every push to master (uses `KAFKA_*`, `TURSO_*` and `HF_TOKEN` secrets). Neither workflow has an `environment:` approval gate or a `permissions:` block. MEDIUM, CI/approvals.
- `.github/workflows/deploy-space.yml:5` — Pushes to master auto-deploy the whole repo to HF Space `swadhinbiswas/eurostream` (line 35) with a long-lived `HF_TOKEN` (line 71). The upload ignores `.git`, `.venv`, `site`, `notes`, `assets` and `data` (line 44). It does not ignore `governance/` or `.env`, and the lines I counted show no `.env*` pattern, so a stray `.env` could be published. There is no approval gate. MEDIUM, CI/long-lived token.
- `.github/workflows/orchestrate.yml:76` — `HF_TOKEN` is passed to the transform step, which has no obvious need for it. Long-lived tokens (HF, Turso, Kafka) are used throughout lines 46-94. MEDIUM, secrets.
- `src/eurostream/config.py:22` — `PII_SALT = "eurostream-pii-salt"` is a hardcoded default. `.env.example:22` ships `EUROSTREAM_PII_SALT=change-me-in-production`. `docker-compose.yml:7-10` does not set the salt, so compose runs use the public default. HIGH, secrets/GDPR (salted hashes are reversible for low-entropy PII).
- `infra/main.tf:59` — S3 encryption is SSE-S3 (`AES256`), not KMS. No KMS resource exists in the IaC, and there is no bucket policy enforcing TLS. LOW/MEDIUM, encryption.
- `infra/main.tf:140` — MSK security-group egress is `0.0.0.0/0` on all protocols. The default for `allowed_client_cidrs` is `10.0.0.0/16` (line 152). MSK at-rest encryption is not configured (lines 114-118 set TLS in transit only). LOW.
- `infra/main.tf:70` — The pipeline role can only be assumed by `ec2.amazonaws.com`. No EC2, ECS or instance profile exists in the IaC, so nothing deployed actually uses the role. The policy itself is scoped to the one bucket with no wildcard actions (lines 88-94), so least privilege is good. INFO.
- `infra/main.tf:103` — MSK is declared as the "deployment target for the bus adapter". The real runtime uses Aiven Kafka (`.env.example:5`, `orchestrate.yml:40`), so the IaC does not match what runs. It is also unusable as-is: `subnet_ids` defaults to `[]` (line 166) and `vpc_id` has no default (line 144). MEDIUM, IaC drift. The header at `infra/main.tf:3` claims "no resource is created outside the EU", but Render, Aiven, Turso, HF, Cloudflare and GitHub are not covered.
- `docker-compose.yml:6` — The compose file maps and health-checks port 8000 (line 15). The Dockerfile `EXPOSE`s 7860 and runs uvicorn on 7860 (`Dockerfile:41,44`). The compose healthcheck will therefore fail. LOW, config bug.
- `render.yaml:5` — `plan: free` with `autoDeploy: true` (line 10) deploys production on every push. `region: frankfurt` (line 6) is EU. The secrets are `sync:false` (dashboard-managed), which is good (lines 14-31).
- `Dockerfile:39` — Runs as non-root user `eurostream`; no finding. The base image `python:3.12-slim` is an unpinned tag (lines 2, 17), and only `src` is copied (line 11), not `governance/`. The `pii_manifest` default path may therefore be missing in the container. LOW.
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml:36` — The `databricks-app` job uses `working-directory: databricks/app` and `databricks/app/package-lock.json` (line 43). The last commit is "chore: remove dbx", so this path may no longer exist and the job may fail. Not verified.

